CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'dcache_dentry_dir_max_sysctl == old'
#121: FILE: fs/dcache.c:206:
+	if (!write || ret || (dcache_dentry_dir_max_sysctl == old))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

WARNING:AVOID_EXTERNS: externs should be avoided in .c files
#161: FILE: kernel/sysctl.c:122:
+extern proc_handler proc_dcache_dentry_dir_max;

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

